course: dictionary
lesson: 3053
title: Eat, and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. To eat is to put food in your mouth, chew it and swallow it. «Tom ate one of the apples» means he took one apple and it is gone. The words around eat show you which meaning fits.
explain: The clues often sit in the next words. «We eat dinner at six» pairs eat with a meal, so it means to have the meal. «Rust eats away metal» pairs eat with away, so it means slowly using up or damaging something. Read the words around eat, then pick the meaning that fits.
explain: Always check by trying your meaning in the sentence. If «rust eats away metal» meant rust chews the metal and swallows it, the sentence would make no sense, so the slow-damage meaning must be right. Context is your check.
fact: Eat is a verb, and its forms are eat, eats, ate, eaten and eating.
fact: «Eat» can mean to put food in your mouth, chew it and swallow it.
fact: «Eat» can mean to have a meal, as in «eat dinner» or «eat out» at a restaurant.
fact: «Eat into» or «eat away» means to slowly use up or damage something, as in «rust eats away metal».
fact: Animals that eat plants are herbivores, and animals that eat meat are carnivores. The thylacine was a striped meat-eating marsupial, so it was a carnivore.
exercise: «Tom ate one of the cakes, so there is one less.» What does ate mean here? | Slowly damaged the cakes | *Put food in his mouth and swallowed it | Ran away with them | Had a meal at a restaurant
exercise: «Rust eats away at the old gate.» What does eats away mean? | *Slowly uses up or damages something | Cleans the gate fast | Eats the gate for dinner | Paints the gate bright red
exercise: «A vulture lands last, bald and scruffy, but it is eating dead animals before their germs can spread.» Find and copy the word that is a form of eat. | animals | *eating | scruffy | bald
test: «Goats nibble paper labels, but they do not really eat tin cans.» What does eat mean here? | To slowly wear away | *Put in the mouth, chew and swallow | To test things with the lips | To nibble only a bit
test: Which of these animals is a carnivore, an animal that eats meat? | A rabbit | A cow | *The thylacine | A goat
exam: Tom says «we eat dinner at six» means we chew the dinner into bits. What is the right meaning? | To cook it at six | To damage the dinner slowly | *To have the meal | To lose the dinner
